       "name": "print(value)",
       "say": "Shows something on the screen. It is how a program talks to you. Hand it text, a number, or the name of a stored value; separate several things with commas. **Watch for:** Text must be in quotes. `print(Hello)` without quotes looks for a box called Hello and fails. **In Excel:** typing a message into a cell",
       "code": "print(\"Hello, data world\")\nprint(\"Total:\", 118)"
